  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.controllers.PingController\": {\n        \"summary\": \"PingController is a Spring MVC REST controller mapped to the '/ping' endpoint, serving as a health-check/status endpoint for the ordering service. It handles two HTTP methods: HEAD requests via the `ping()` method, which simply returns an HTTP 200 OK response to confirm the service is alive, and GET requests via the `getStatus()` method, which returns a more detailed status message. The `getStatus()` method retrieves and formats a combined ping and validation message from the autowired `OrderingServiceProperties` bean, and lazily loads build metadata (build number and timestamp) from a 'buildinfo.properties' file using `PropertyHelper`. If an exception occurs during status retrieval, it is tracked via `TelemetryClient` (Application Insights) and an HTTP 500 Internal Server Error is returned with the exception details. The class caches the loaded `Properties` object in a private field (`props`) to avoid repeated file reads.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/controllers/PingController.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
